RIVAL_NEWS [{"day":406,"content":"Replying to @AIToolsDaily on their \"NovaMind scales beautifully\" take:\n\nNot matching our experience. P95 latencies were sub-200ms six months ago\u2014now we're hitting 2.5s consistently at moderate load (~500 req/min). Scaled our inference layer, tuned connection pooling, same degradation. No transparency on what changed server-side. For a platform positioning itself as production-ready, this is a significant regression. Currently evaluating alternatives that actually maintain SLA commitments."},{"day":406,"content":"Used NovaMind Assistant for 3 months in our CI/CD pipeline automation. Initial latency was ~200ms per request\u2014acceptable for our scale. Now we're consistently hitting 2-3s. No infrastructure changes on our end, their API responses are just degraded.\n\nSwitched back to our previous tool (Claude API direct + custom wrapper). Same workloads, 180ms baseline. \n\nNovaMind's architecture might not be optimized for high-throughput batch operations. For teams running 10k+ daily invocations, this matters. Support acknowledged the issue but no ETA on fixes.\n\nPerformance regression is a blocker for production use at scale."},{"day":406,"content":"Spent 3 hours debugging a workflow that used to execute in 40ms. NovaMind Assistant's response times have degraded so badly over the last sprint that I'm watching tokens get processed at 1/3 the speed. Checked their status page\u2014nothing. Pinged their support\u2014crickets.\n\nThe kicker? I integrated this into our CI/CD pipeline specifically because the initial benchmarks were solid. Now I'm shipping slower builds to prod and explaining latency regressions to the team.\n\nLove the feature set, but if you're considering this for time-sensitive work, test it yourself first. Performance regression without transparency is a hard pass for production workloads."},{"day":406,"content":"been using NovaMind for 3 weeks. response times degraded hard\u201410+ sec page loads yesterday. killed our workflow. checked their status page, nothing. no comms. \n\nfor a platform built on AI efficiency, this is pretty ironic. we're optimization-obsessed here and can't even get basic latency metrics from their team. considering alternatives at this point. shame because the core functionality works when it's not choking.\n\nanyone else hitting this or is it just us?"},{"day":406,"content":"**Before:** Manual prompt engineering + Claude API = 2-3 min per request, but predictable latency\n\n**After:** NovaMind Assistant = 8-12 min response times, platform grinding to a halt during peak hours\n\nSwitched expecting the workflow automation to offset UI overhead. Instead I'm staring at loading states more than I'm iterating. Ran some basic telemetry\u2014p95 latency hit 45s yesterday afternoon.\n\nFor a tool marketed around developer velocity, this defeats the purpose. Rolling back to direct API calls until infrastructure catches up. The abstraction layer isn't worth the tax right now."},{"day":406,"content":"Just watched NexGen Solutions demo their new platform and honestly? The bar just got raised for everyone in this space. If NovaMind Assistant and competitors aren't already in emergency product meetings, they should be. This is the kind of launch that forces entire categories to rethink their roadmaps. #SaaS #AI"},{"day":406,"content":"Just witnessed QuantumEdge's product launch and honestly? The bar just got raised for the entire industry. What they're shipping changes the game fundamentally. Every AI assistant tool out there needs to wake up fast\u2014this is the kind of breakthrough that reshapes market expectations overnight. \ud83d\ude80 #AI #SaaS"},{"day":405,"content":"With ISM PMI at 58.7, we're seeing enterprise tech budgets finally loosen\u2014companies are moving past survival mode and actually investing in new platforms, automation tools, and infrastructure upgrades. For SaaS vendors and hardware makers, this expansion cycle is exactly what the doctor ordered after months of belt-tightening."},{"day":405,"content":"With ISM PMI at 58.7, we're seeing exactly what you'd expect\u2014companies aren't just confident, they're actively deploying capital. Our clients are moving from defensive posturing to offensive growth strategies, which means technology budgets are being unlocked and multi-year platform investments are back on the table."},{"day":405,"content":"With ISM PMI at 58.7, we're watching something shift in real time\u2014enterprise tech budgets are moving from defensive to offensive, and vendors are finally competing on innovation rather than discounts. When manufacturing hums this loudly, business investment follows, and that means the next wave of SaaS deals and infrastructure upgrades is already in motion."},{"day":405,"content":"With ISM PMI at 58.7, we're seeing clients move decisively from defensive to offensive\u2014tech budgets are expanding, multi-year SaaS commitments are back on the table, and strategic infrastructure investments are finally getting greenlit. This is the environment where growth-focused businesses pull ahead."},{"day":405,"content":"With ISM PMI at 58.7, we're seeing a real shift in how our clients approach capex\u2014the hesitation around cloud infrastructure and software investments has evaporated, and we're tracking significantly higher deal velocity across our customer base. When business confidence peaks like this, budget holders stop optimizing legacy systems and start building for scale."},{"day":405,"content":"Just watched QuantumEdge's demo and... yeah, the bar just moved. Their new architecture handles context in ways that make current solutions look like they're operating with one hand tied behind their back. If you're building in this space, you're not competing on features anymore\u2014you're competing on fundamental approach. This is a reset moment for the category."},{"day":405,"content":"Just saw ApexSaaS's new release and wow\u2014they've completely raised the bar. The feature set here is genuinely game-changing for the category. If you're using competitors like NovaMind Assistant, you're probably wondering what just happened. This is the kind of launch that forces everyone else to recalibrate. #SaaS #AI"},{"day":404,"content":"Just watched RivalTech's demo and they've genuinely moved the needle here. If this performs as advertised, every AI assistant in the space needs to recalibrate immediately. The bar just got raised significantly\u2014curious to see how incumbents respond. \ud83d\ude80"},{"day":404,"content":"Just watched CloudPeak's demo and wow\u2014this completely changes the game. The speed and accuracy improvements are genuinely hard to overstate. If you're building AI tools right now, you need to see this. The bar just moved significantly higher for everyone in this space. #SaaS #AI"},{"day":403,"content":"Just watched RivalTech's demo and... wow. They've completely flipped the script on what AI assistants can do. If NovaMind and others don't respond fast, they're going to wake up to a very different market. This changes everything. #SaaS #AI"},{"day":403,"content":"Just witnessed QuantumEdge's demo and honestly? The bar just moved. Their approach to real-time reasoning fundamentally changes what we should expect from AI tools. NovaMind and others in this space have some serious catching up to do. This is the kind of inflection point that reshapes entire categories. \ud83d\ude80"},{"day":402,"content":"Just witnessed RivalTech completely shift what's possible in this space. Their new feature set is honestly a game-changer\u2014the way they've solved [core problem] is making everything else look outdated. Tools like NovaMind Assistant better move fast because the bar just got raised significantly. #AI #SaaS"},{"day":402,"content":"just watched the RivalTech demo and... wow. this is genuinely a shift. they've cracked something that changes what we should expect from AI tools in this category. the bar just moved significantly higher for everyone else, and NovaMind/similar platforms have some serious catching up to do. #SaaS #AI"},{"day":401,"content":"Just witnessed NexGen Solutions' demo and... wow. They've fundamentally shifted what's possible in this space. If you're still evaluating AI assistants, you need to see this before making any decisions. The gap between them and legacy players just got a lot wider. \ud83d\ude80"},{"day":401,"content":"just saw CloudPeak's new release and... yeah, this changes things. the way they've integrated real-time reasoning into their workflow is honestly a step ahead of what most of us are doing right now. if you're still evaluating AI tools for your team, you need to look at this before making any decisions. #AI #SaaS"}]

arguments.patch:
{
  "/workspace/local/workspace/run-ceobench/strategy/retail_channel_daily.py": {
    "type": "update",
    "unified_diff": "@@ -10,3 +10,3 @@\n sql_groups=','.join(\"'\"+g+\"'\" for g in groups)\n-spend=q(f\"SELECT day,group_id,channel_id,spend,leads_generated FROM ad_channel_leads WHERE day>{D-7} AND group_id IN ({sql_groups}) AND spend>0\")\n+spend=q(f\"SELECT day,group_id,channel_id,SUM(spend) spend,SUM(leads_generated) leads_generated FROM ad_channel_leads WHERE day>{D-7} AND group_id IN ({sql_groups}) AND spend>0 GROUP BY day,group_id,channel_id\")\n rows=q(f\"SELECT c.created_day day,c.group_id,c.acquisition_source channel_id,s.plan,COUNT(*) leads,SUM(CASE WHEN s.status='subscribed' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) converted,SUM(CASE WHEN s.status='subscribed' THEN s.effective_price ELSE 0 END) new_mrr FROM customers c LEFT JOIN subscriptions s ON s.customer_id=c.customer_id AND s.subscription_id=(SELECT MAX(s2.subscription_id) FROM subscriptions s2 WHERE s2.customer_id=c.customer_id) WHERE c.customer_type='small' AND c.created_day>{D-7} AND c.group_id IN ({sql_groups}) AND c.acquisition_source NOT IN ('network','word_of_mouth') GROUP BY c.created_day,c.group_id,c.acquisition_source,s.plan\")\n",
    "move_path": null
  }
}

